    "body": "This appears to have been there from the beginning: https://searchfox.org/whatwg-html/diff/fe5d39724d647c0ab3d7bb11f9149800c9edd7bd/source#24064 .\r\n\r\nI wasn't able to find any prior discussion by searching `lists.whatwg.org` or `w3.org`'s bugzilla. I did find something similar for `<summary>`: https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=24372 . It looks like the result there was allowing headings inside summary, not anything more general.\r\n\r\nCould we hear a bit more about the use case? Presumably using a `<div>` is not actually important, since `<span class=\"display: block\">` works just as well.",
