    "updated_at": "2023-09-08T01:44:10Z",
    "body": "In particular it's not clear what we would open this up to. For example, allowing headings inside buttons seems wrong. Similar for a variety of other elements like `<noscript>`, `<map>`, `<dialog>`. Sectioning content maybe? But probably not?\r\n\r\nSo this leads me to suspect the answer is \"because phrasing content is the most natural existing category of things that make sense inside a button\". If there are use cases for more specific categories, like we saw with headings inside `<summary>`, then probably we would expand on a case-by-case basis, still starting with phrasing content as the base.",
