    "updated_at": "2023-09-08T08:03:53Z",
    "body": "We changed `<a>` model so you could make a clickable box (e.g., containing a heading, an image, and a description), which is a somewhat common UI pattern or at least used to be. Making such content a button feels like a stretch, but maybe? I'd love to see some actual examples.",
