    "created_at": "2023-09-08T17:36:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-08T17:36:28Z",
    "body": "Thanks for all of the comments and history here. This issue was opened because I had a conversation with someone who asked why they couldn't put a `<div>` inside the button. Perhaps a baby-step in this direction is to just expand to \"phrasing content or a `<div>`\"? I do see the points about other semantic element types being at least odd if not problematic. E.g. `<button><h1>`. But perhaps a non-semantic element like `<div>` which people tend to just reach for as the default structural block element would not cause problems?\r\n\r\nI tend to agree with [this comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9705#issuecomment-1711207646) - having rules in the validator that error out when there's no \"good\" reason to have a limitation leads to people ignore the validator. Additionally, it's actively helpful to developers to guide them away from things that are actually bad (e.g. `<button><h1>`) and let them do things that don't appear to cause harm (`<button><div>`).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
