    "created_at": "2025-02-16T09:32:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-18T13:12:34Z",
    "body": "Relaxing this rule would also be helpful from an accessibility perspective. Interactive elements that contain block elements cannot use the <button> element directly. This often forces developers to use a very cumbersome workaround like this to make the element accessible:\n\n```html\n<div\n    tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" onclick=\"onClick()\"\n    onkeydown=\"handleKeyDown(event)\"\n>\n    Button without button\n</div>\n\n<script>\nfunction onClick() {\n  console.log(\"Clicked!\");\n}\n\nfunction handleKeyDown(event) {\n    if (event.key === \"Enter\" || event.key === \" \") {\n        onClick();\n    }\n}\n</script>\n```\nThe idea with HTML 5 was to make HTML semantic. Limiting child elements based on layout properties is going against this idea.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
